Package: ivserial
Type: Package
Title: Exact Symbolic Tests of Serial Independence
Version: 1.0.2
Authors@R: person("Emad", "Ashtari Nezhad", email = "emaad7@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-6779-4742"))
Description: Rank-based tests of the hypothesis that a time series is a
    sequence of independent and identically distributed values. The values
    are replaced by quantile classes; a block statistic compares the
    frequencies of patterns of consecutive classes with their expected values
    and a portmanteau does the same for pairs at several lags. The combined
    test is calibrated exactly by random permutations, so its P-value is
    valid for every sample size and every continuous distribution. The
    package also gives the asymptotic weighted chi-square null distribution,
    a serial Cramer coefficient of dependence between 0 and 1, the patterns
    responsible for a rejection, sample-size and power calculations, the
    screening of many series with false discovery rate control, and a
    graphical interface. The procedure is that of Ashtari Nezhad, Information
    Variance and Exact Symbolic Tests of Serial Independence (manuscript).
